  "notes": [
    "Maximums and minimums are per 1,000 points unless otherwise stated (p. 109). The builder applies them as written, which is right for armies up to 1,000 points; scale them up yourself for larger armies.",
    "Divisional batteries go in an infantry brigade of the same nationality, and Horse batteries with a cavalry brigade; build them as their own entries here and deploy them with the brigade.",
    "Detached Light Companies: the Line battalions of a British or KGL brigade can lose their Light companies (and with them Mixed Formation). Two battalions' companies make a Tiny unit, three or four a Small unit, for any infantry brigade. Not built here.",
    "Rockets and howitzers: one Horse battery per army can be exchanged for a rocket battery (Black Powder p. 84), and one battery for a smoothbore field howitzer battery (p. 80). An Artillery Brigade can't have more 9-pounder than 6-pounder batteries. Not built here.",
    "The brigade boxes price a Small Rifle company at 48, Household Cavalry at 61 and a Dragoon Guard regiment at 49; the stat table says 47, 58 and 47, which the builder uses.",
    "Half batteries cost what the Options boxes take off (Royal 15, Horse 17, Hanoverian 13), with the half battery stat line on p. 108 (2-1-1, Stamina 1).",
    "Named commanders have no official points cost in this supplement; they're priced here at the Divisional Commander cost for their Staff Rating, so adjust as you agree."
  ],
  "specialRules": [
    "Cannot Form Attack Column: British, KGL and Hanoverian Field infantry can only form Line, Four-Deep Line, Column of Companies, Mixed Formation, March Column or Square. They can still break into skirmish order to enter terrain they couldn't normally, and form Attack Column in built-up areas. Hanoverian Landwehr can form Attack Column.",
    "Must Form Square: British, KGL and Hanoverian infantry.",
    "Four-Deep Line: three bases wide and two deep; −1 Shooting and −1 Hand-to-Hand, doesn't count as a column (no +1 to be hit by artillery), keeps Steady Line and First Fire and can form Mixed Formation.",
    "Column of Companies: one company wide (four bases deep). +1 Staff Rating to order it; shoots with one die; −2 Hand-to-Hand; counts as an Attack Column when shot at by artillery but gets no Morale bonus for it.",
    "Rifle Mixed Formation: as Mixed Formation (Black Powder p. 78), but the shot counts as from a rifle.",
    "Lie Down: a battalion ordered to Lie Down makes artillery re-roll hits on it at medium and long range, but is dispersed if contacted. Any army's infantry can do this.",
    "Deep Formation (all cavalry): two bases wide, three deep. +1 Staff Rating to order it, +1 combat resolution, −1 Hand-to-Hand, and artillery gets +1 to hit it.",
    "Ferocious Charge and Gallop at Anything: British cavalry suffer +2 on their Command roll when they leave the table. Gallop at Anything gives +1 to Charge orders and Ferocious Charge, but the unit must make a breakthrough move if allowed, even off the table.",
    "Shrapnel: British guns can fire at medium range with 3 dice, but need 5s to hit."
  ],
